INSERT INTO `news` VALUES (15,'Inflation with deflation reports','2011-09-16 21:42:54','The reports keep saying that the inflation is low in the US. However, everywhere around the world are crying so loud about inflation. \n\n\n\nAs customers, all we know that inflation is really high. It is not as what the announcing report saying.',1,'tom'),(17,'What happen to the arab world','2011-09-16 22:16:05','After the war in Iraq, they suddenly realize that strong religion spirit is not enough to complete with advance technologies. When everyone wants to be changed, the revolution is beginning.',2,'tom'),(18,'Election year is coming.','2011-09-17 01:46:56','Usually, a president can be elected for two term. However, the house representatives have more republican. The house has more reflection what the major American feel.  ',0,'tom'),(19,'Zero percent interest rate: really hurt anyone around','2011-09-17 02:08:14','Inflation without income growth is not possible to pull this economy out the storm. Eventually everyone are short with money somehow or another.',1,'tom'),(23,'Competition heat up in the smart phone world','2011-10-09 02:26:29','Apple has the great run in the last few years and dominate the whole smart phone sector.  Google tries to spend its cash to control the operation system of the phone.  Both companies have a lot of cash. It is interesting to watch who will be at the end.',1,'tom'),(24,'Halloween','2011-11-02 21:16:52','Beside the pumpkins and masks, after all it is children’s holiday. Usually, for some kind of reasons, the parents are not buying candies for their kids all time. But Halloween is a free candy day.  As long as a child not shy enough to prevent him/her to walk by any stores and say “trick or treat”, a free candy on its way. It is pack of children from age of zero to the teens with costumes around my neighborhood very year during Halloween.',0,'tom'),(26,'远望中国','2011-11-02 21:21:24','过去的三十年,中国发展的真不错, 最起马能使一个从充满饥饿的国家, 到一个生活过得去, 同时又不受外来势力压迫的国家.\n\n我是亲眼见到同感受到这些变化的, 三十年前, 人们生活非常艰苦, 能吃饱还有问题, 能穿上一对新鞋就非常高兴. 现在就不用\n\n多说了, 基本生活都满足. \n\n\n\n不要忘记了, 中国是农民的天下, 老百姓才是主人. 不信, 翻开一九四九年十月一日, 毛泽东回应人民时说的那句话: \n\n\"人民万岁\".   \"土改\", \"资产阶级斗争\", \"文化大革命\", 那一样不是为农民着想的呢？\n\n\n\n最近总是听到一些新闻关于某某地方反对政府是因为土地挣夺. 这些事情看起来很简单. 可是很相似皇朝时代的土豪与地方官互\n\n相勾结来压迫老百姓.',0,'tom'),(27,'近看美国','2011-11-02 21:23:50','美国还是最富有的国家,我说的是最多富有人的国家,而且非常富有, 当然不是说政府.\n\n非常可笑, 富人把政府的钱变为己有, 再逼使普通的民众去还.',0,'tom'),(28,'0% rate to boot up economy','2011-11-03 01:27:25','Can anyone borrow money from the banks these days? The banks can borrow a lot of money from FED with 0% rate and use the depositors’ money with almost 0% payout.  All the operations the FED are doing right now is to put a lot of money into the bankers’ hands, and hope the bankers to lend out more money.  As you can see that our economy is on the hands’ of bankers again.  The banks benefit the most from this low rate.  The major asset of the banks\' portfolios are real estates and stocks which they aquired during the house bubble. Low rate is good for both of this kind of assets.  ',0,'tom'),(29,'Good news','2011-11-07 17:00:12','Good news are comming.',1,'tom'),(30,'Holiday is coming','2011-11-08 02:27:38','Share something you have, to make everyone around you happier, to make a better world.',0,'tom'),(34,'Greek Debt','2011-11-17 05:06:32','Greece is not major country of the Europe, but why its debt affects the market globally? The answer is in the high school history text book. World War I started off from Europe because of the conflict between European countries about the colonies. Then World War II started off because of the debt of the World War I.  Do you get it?  This is all about debt or money again. Greek debt is not dangerous at all, but how different countries react to it differently reflect the dangerousness.',1,'jessica'),(35,'经济的真相','2011-11-16 04:56:44','中国政府于2008年下半年推出“四万亿刺激经济计划” 的真正原因是对抗人民币升值.',0,'jessica'),(36,'地产泡沬','2011-11-16 05:12:38','可是中国银行受到别国银行的影向把钱全投向地产, 使地产生成泡沬',0,'jessica'),(37,'When will the winter come?','2011-11-16 06:01:42','It is warm. When will it snow? That is what my daughter complains all the time this year. The weather is kind warm this year again. Comparing twenty years ago, the weather is really warmer than before. Also, there are many floods in the Asia. It seems that global warming do has some kind of effect.',0,'jessica'),(38,'图书馆借书逾期 捐食物可抵罚款','2011-11-20 23:29:56','在图书馆有借书逾期罚款的民众有「将功赎罪」的机会，今年圣马刁县县立图书馆推出「食品换罚款」计划，民众只要在12月间带着可存放的食品到图书馆捐献，逾期罚款就可一笔勾销，去年这项计划募得超过3万磅食品。 \n\n',0,'tom'),(39,'Fees for parking meter','2012-01-31 00:43:46','I took a trip with my children to the Washington DC last spring. Since there are so many tourists, so it is hard to find a parking spot around parks. We tried to walk from our hotel to different places except the last day because it was really tired for children after walking for a few days.  We tried to wake up very early in the morning and drive the car around.  We did able to find a meter parking pot which is cost 25 cents for 7 minutes. I suddenly realize that the charge is more expansive than in NYC. It usually costs 25 cents for 10 minutes in NYC.  How can be, NYC usually the most expansive place around the world?<br/>\r\n<p/>\r\nNew York City, especially downtown Manhattan, it is impossible to find a meter parking spot during the weekdays. Instead of driving there, I took subways there for more than one year.  Recently, since my mom has joint pain on one of her leg, it is really hard to her to walk around. No other options, I have to drive her there to see the doctor, guess what? The parking meter fee had been raised. It is 50 cents for 10 minutes! Indeed, NYC is still most expansive city in the world.\r\n',0,'tom'),(40,'Complations of the FED','2012-02-13 16:57:54','<p>Only one kind of person does not like the Fed, the big saver. Others should ignore the media and enjoy what the Fed did for our country.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nAs everyone should know, so far the Fed dumps as much as possible money currency into the market circulation including through the banks, stock market, treasury back backs. That could cause many outcomes. There are few things could and expect to be happen in the future:\r\n</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>	Inflation. Many people think that inflation is bad, actually, if you are business owners, you know that inflation is great environment to do business because you able to sell your stuff more expansive. The revenues and the margins will go up at the same time. For example, if you own a candy store, you bought the candy for $0.50 and resell it for $0.75. Then you make $0.25 for profit.  Because of the inflation, you able to sell the same candy for $1.00. Then you make $0.50 for the same candy.\r\n</li>\r\n<li>As everyone know that our government has more than $15 trillions of debt. Most of this debt is owned by the foreign governments. We need to pay them back in some ways. Usually, in order to pay off the personal debt, a person needs to work hard to earn some money to pay off the debt. However, the Fed prints the money to pay off the debt. As American citizen you should not complain about this.\r\n</li>\r\n<li> Since the debt only has fixed value and very low fixed interest income every year, once a lot of paper money is printed, the value of debt become lower, so that it is easier to pay off in the future inflation environment.\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Inflation is bad for the savers too, especially for the big savers. Who are the big savers? Of course not a regular person with a few thousands in the money market account.  The big savers are corporations with billions of cash in their accounts. With almost 0% gain per year, these companies will be forced to invest their cash to generate a better return. Otherwise, the money will take away by the printing process a little by little. Either this money will be used to improve their companies or offer new services; consequently, more people will be hired for expansions.  Unemployed people should be happy and not complain about the Fed too.\r\n</li>\r\n<li>The pension funds also benefit from this low rate environment. The super riches will not put the money on the bonds anymore, and keep their money in the stock market which the pension funds held most of value. The baby boomer generations are closed to the retirement ages. The government cannot afford to deal the shortage of the pension funds.  As long as the person funds with the money to pay their obligations, the baby boomers should not complain about it.\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n',0,'tom'),(41,'So many things are monopolies nowadays','2012-02-15 05:21:52','I usually go to do shopping once every month to buy all general basic house items such as toilet papers, tooth paste  and baby milks. Every time I go to the toilet paper section in the store, all the toilet papers are made by two companies ever there are more than two brands. I have no other choices. I must pick one of them even the prices of both have been raised recently. Same thing happen to infants milks, there are only two brands.  The internet service providers in my neighborhood also only have two companies available. I believe there are many monopolies around if you look around.',0,'jessica'),(42,'Dividend money have been taxes twice','2012-02-16 03:42:21','\"Dividend money have been taxes twice, they should be taxed only 15% for income\". \"Taxed twice\" is try to fool the public and get the tax loophole for super rich again. They said that this money has been taxed as corporation income, and they own the company, the company income tax consider of one time of tax, and personal income tax as another time of tax. That is not the right way to say that, they just try to fool the public. The real meaning of this law is like that, if you own the company, you only pay 15% for your income tax no matter how much you make. However, this law does not apply to all the private companies\' owners whom also own their companies. They all have been taxed as high as top bracket. What about the employees of the companies, they are the ones who actually make money for the company, not the stock holders. All the employees\' incomes also are taxed twice then. Should they also get only 15% on their income taxes too? By looking back how this law was passed, it is really sad too, it was added to the extended  unemployment packages as a string during the tech bubble. In order to stop the public to complain about it, the package also allowed the congress to mail every tax payer a check about $500. But because of this  law, the super riches save millions, or billions on their income taxes every years. How can our government debt not getting higher and higher.',0,'jessica'),(43,'What is wrong to be rich?','2012-02-16 03:44:11','\"What is wrong to be rich?\" of course, nothing is wrong to be rich. All of us want to be rich. However, how people get rich should be matter. Otherwise, it is ok to get rich by criminals. Creating laws to pay less tax for himself/herself is not right thing to do. How can a congressman who supposes to work for this country, but create laws to be benefited for himself/herself to be good? Getting rich by creating something that improves our country or the civilization, I don\'t think anybody has any questions about it.',0,'jessica'),(45,'Many parks have been reconstructed in NYC','2010-07-16 02:53:45','We are in the park now. My kids are playing. I am feeling a little tired because of yesterday\'s trip to the liberty.  Instead of moving around, sitting on the bench and watching the children running around.  It is in the middle of the summer. Luckily, this little park near the shore is covered by the trees.  It is kind of cool when the wind blows through from time to time.  The small water fountain in the children\'s playground is also on. Many children are playing with the water. My older daughter keeps sneaking through the water fountain and run to me by yelling loud excitedly that she is wet.  It is kind of surprised to me that she so active because she usually is shy in the public place.',0,'tom'),(46,'Apps on the phones','2012-02-29 16:36:45','apps on the phone is kind of new, five years ago was not much. I believe that there are security issues on the phone related to the apps. For example, after I add the email account to the phone. All my contacts are transferred to my email providers. When I login to my account from the internet, i can see all my contacts data from my phone. That means all personal contacts had been stored in the emails provider\'s database. The worse part is that all internet email are not encrypted. Beside the provider, other parties are able see all your personal contacts as long as your request pages go through their servers.',0,'tom'),(47,'500 billion, Apple','2012-02-29 17:05:01','$500,000,000,000\n\nDon\'t worry, compare to our debt $15 trillion debt=15,000,000,000,000, not much.\n\n\n\n<p/> Please remember the following number, we are getting there someday <br/>10^6 = a million<br/>10^9 = billion\n<br/>10^12 = trillion\n<br/>10^15 = quadrillion\n<br/>10^18 = quintillion\n<br/>10^21 = sextillion\n<br/>10^24 = septillion\n<br/>10^27 = octillion<br/>\n10^30 = nonillion</br>\n10^33 = decillion</br>',0,'jessica'),(48,'Mosquitoes In New York City','2012-04-18 03:06:22','Mosquitoes, mosquitoes and mosquitoes, a lot of mosquitoes, that was what my daughters told me when we had a picnic in one of  New York upstate park this Easter. Suddenly, I realize that, in the last few years, not just in upstate, there are a lot of Mosquitoes in New York City too. It became so obvious last year, my children’s legs had big red bites from the mosquitoes every time we opened the windows and forgot to close them at night. \r\n\r\nSpring just arrives in New York, a lot of people have allergy. Hopefully, it will not have that many mosquitoes this summer.  \r\n',0,'tom'),(49,'Seven things keep you thinking','2012-04-18 04:18:54','<ol>\r\n\r\n<li>Debt = Dead, they sound the same, they treat people the same too. </li>\r\n\r\n<li>Give a person a fish, he only eats fish once. Teach a person how to catch fishes, he will eat fish for the rest of his life.\r\n</li>\r\n\r\n<li> $1,000,000 is more or a magic penny that will double your money  from a penny by one month.</br>\r\n1 day: 1 cent<br/>\r\n2 day: 2 cent<br/>\r\n3 day: 4 cent<br/>\r\n4 day: 8 cent<br/>\r\n5 day: 16 cent<br/>\r\n6 day: 32 cent<br/>\r\n7 day: 64 cent<br/>\r\n8 day: $1.28<br/>\r\n9 day: $2.56<br/>\r\n10 day: $5.12<br/>\r\n11 day: $10.24<br/>\r\n12 day: $20.48<br/>\r\n13 day: $40.96<br/>\r\n14 day: $81.92<br/>\r\n15 day: $163.84<br/>\r\n16 day: $327.68<br/>\r\n17 day: $655.36<br/>\r\n18 day: $1,310.72<br/>\r\n19 day: $2,621.44<br/>\r\n20 day: $5,242.88<br/>\r\n21 day: $10,485.76<br/>\r\n22 day: $20,971.52<br/>\r\n23 day: $41,943.04<br/>\r\n24 day: $83,886.08<br/>\r\n25 day: $167,772.16<br/>\r\n26 day: $335,544.32<br/>\r\n27 day: $671,088.64<br/>\r\n28 day: $1,342,177.28<br/>\r\n29 day: $2,684,354.56<br/>\r\n30 day: $5,368,709.12<br/>\r\n</li>\r\n\r\n<li>Rule 72: how long does it take to double your money? \r\n<p>You don’t need to understand the math behind it. All you need to know the percentage you gain from your money from a certain period.</p>\r\n<p>For example: If you have $1000 you put it on 6% one year CD(of course, this is magic number this day), you will double your money by this rule: 72 / 6  = 12 years. The 72 is from the Rule 72, 6 is from the 6% rate. If you divided 72 by the rate number, That is how much time you need to double your money.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>The banks use this rule  to calculate how much they make when they give your mortgages too. If you got a loan for 6% for 15 years. You actually pay them double of the loan amount by the 12th year(72/6=12).</p>\r\n</li>\r\n\r\n<li>Live under your means: find out what it means by searching on the internet.</li>\r\n\r\n<li>.Rich is not equal wealthy</li>\r\n<li>Time is more valuable than gold.</li>\r\n</ol>',0,'tom'),(50,'不要秋后算账','2012-04-24 04:42:31','台湾总统刚下台, 就马上进入监牢, 泰国以前的总理也是如此, 而差不多每一届韩国总统都追究法律责任, 菲律宾的总统更不用说.  一个本来受人拥护总统, 刚下台, 就受某种追究. 真让人觉得, 为了权力斗争, 而秋后算账.',0,'jessica'),(51,'The Streets are quiet in the morning','2012-05-02 04:03:22','That means good news. A lot of people get back to work again. Not that many jobless people hang out on the street anymore.',0,'tom'),(52,'The gas price is more expansive than milk','2012-05-02 04:10:43','It does not make sense to me at all. We need a strike for the gas price too high. Let\'s all stop driving the cars for one week, let the price drops back to $1/gal. ',0,'jessica'),(53,'The Riches and the Poors','2012-05-24 13:31:49','What about the middle guy? so far, there is someone fight for the poors, and the riches have their own money to fight for them. For example, the expansive meter parking spot, the poor don\'t driving the cars around because they can not offer it, and the riches never park in the meter, they only park their cars in the garages. Therefore, all this parking meters are only made up for the middle guys. This is only a very simple example. Many things around like that these days.',0,'tom'),(56,'The main reason of high electric bill','2012-05-27 03:47:30','<p>My electric bill went up about 40% since the beginning of 2010 and it never went back to the price I paid before. I did called Con Edison, my electricity company to find out what is going on? They said that I used more electricity than before.  However, I only added one extra computer in the house that year, nothing else. I did some searching on the internet to figure out how much electricity a single computer uses for one hour. The result told me that the electricity usage of one computer is not possible to push my bill up 40%.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nI get my electric bill today, May 2012, but the amount on the bill is little bit lower than previous month, I am wondering what is going on again. Therefore, I take a close look at my bill again and do some searching on the internet again.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nGuess what I find out:\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nThe electric bill has two kinds of charges:  Delivery charge and Supply charge. \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nThe total of bill = delivery charges + supply charges\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nThe delivery charge is fully controlled by Con Edison since the electricity system is monopoly. However, Con Edison cannot raise the delivery charge whatever they want since the electricity system is regulated. That means, in order to raise the price, Con Edison must have the permission from the local government.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nAccording to this articles <a href=\'http://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2009/01/07/con-ed-rate-increase-moves-forward/\'> http://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2009/01/07/con-ed-rate-increase-moves-forward</a> and <a href=\'http://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2009/04/21/regulators-approve-con-edison-rate-increase/\'> http://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2009/04/21/regulators-approve-con-edison-rate-increase/</a>, the local government give the permission to Con Edison to raise the delivery charge.  The interesting question is why the local government gave the permission to Con Edison to raise the price?  The main reason was the blackout and the explosion event before the permission is granted.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nCon Edison said that it was hard to maintain a reliable system without raise the delivery fee. That is why there are blackouts. So obviously, if the local government does not allow it to raise the price, it will let you have the blackouts. \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nAnother interesting question, why Con Edison needs to and wants to raise the delivery charge? The main reason is the supply charge. Since the supply charge of the electricity is not monopoly, Con Edison has to complete with other suppliers, therefore, Con Edison unable to raise the supply charges to make as much profit as before.  In order to make up the same profit as before, Con Edison use the blackouts to force the local government to grant the permission to raise the delivery charges to make up the profit from the lost of supply charges.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nI compare my old bills from the year of 2008 and the bill of 2012, the supply charge is little bit lower, but the delivery charges is up more than 40%. As everyone knows, the supply charge is related to the price of commodities. Since the supply charge does not change that much, therefore, the increase price of commodities does not cause the increase our electric bills.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nFinally, I realize that, it is not the extra computer I got, it is not the blackout, it is not the increase price of the commodities make our electricity bills so high, it is the delivery charge which is monopoly. \r\n</p>\r\n',0,'complainer'),(57,'Current Calendar System does not refer the seasons anymore','2013-02-28 14:04:45','One year has four seasons. The seasons start from spring, summer, fall and winter each year.  \r\n\r\nTherefore, from January to March is spring, but the weather still cold outside with 30F.\r\n\r\nIt is still winter.\r\n',0,'May');
