rced perfect terminators. Picking the right terminator is vital to the performance of your SCSI chain. A passive terminator is simply a resistor network that regulates the impedance in the line, while an active terminator uses a voltage regulator to optimize signal voltage. Active termination is always preferred over passive, and most of our active terminators feature an LED to monitor terminator power line status. Make the right connection with Cables To Go! Connector 1: 50-pin IDC Male',30.99,'Adapters or Connectors','Internal SCSI-1/SCSI-2 IDC50M Active Terminator','Lifetime','Qualify for Free shiipping after the total order is more than $30','2012-06-01 15:27:51','tom',0,10,10,3,40,3.00,15.13),(3572,'757120035725','cable','We offer a wide variety of SCSI terminators to optimize the performance of your SCSI bus, from the popular passive and active terminators for single-ended SCSI applications, to the active negation and hard-to-find, premium-quality forced perfect terminators. Picking the right terminator is vital to the performance of your SCSI chain. A passive terminator is simply a resistor network that regulates the impedance in the line, while an active terminator uses a voltage regulator to optimize signal voltage. Active termination is always preferred over passive, and most of our active terminators feature an LED to monitor terminator power line status. Make the right connection with Cables To Go! Functionally equivalent to Sunandreg #150-1785.Connector 1: Micro-Density 50 Male with Latches',30.99,'Adapters or Connectors','External SCSI-2 MD50M Active Terminator','Lifetime','Qualify for Free shiipping after the total order is more than $30','2012-06-01 15:27:51','tom',0,10,10,3,47,3.00,10.40),(3574,'757120035749','cable','We offer a wide variety of SCSI terminators to optimize the performance of your SCSI bus, from the popular passive and active terminators for single-ended SCSI applications, to the active negation and hard-to-find, premium-quality forc