,'tom',0,10,10,3,32,3.00,20.50),(42119,'757120421191','cable','RapidRun is known for its versatility, convenience and ease of installation. However, even the most experienced installers will run into hazards that damage or kink the cable during installation. Problems associated with installation damage are seldom found until the final phase of the installation when the cable is already enclosed in the wall. Color-coded blue for use with RapidRun Multimedia runners, this test adapter lets an installer run a quick continuity test of the Multimedia runner to ensure proper functionality BEFORE the installer leaves the job site. This test adapter includes two pieces: a modified RapidRun connector that connects to the display end of the runner, and an RJ45 adapter cable that connects to the input of a common network cable tester (#26846).Instructions For Use:andbull; Attach the modified RapidRun connector to the display end of the Multimedia runner cable.andbull; Connect the network tester to the source end of the runner cable using the RJ45 adapter cable.andbull; Run a continuity test on the cable.andbull; Pins 4 and 5 should show as a short on the test readout.andbull; If you do not get this readout, please contact your RapidRun sales representative for assistance, or call customer service at 1-800-506-9607..',29.99,'RapidRun','1ft RapidRun(R) Multimedia Runner Cable (Blue) Test Adapter Cable','Lifetime','Qualify for Free shiipping after the total order is more than $30','2012-06-01 15:27:51','tom',0,10,10,3,33,3.00,20.50),(42123,'757120421238','cable','RapidRun(R) is designed to be the standard for in-wall audio/video installations. The RapidRun system empowers you to customize your installation to create your own ideal audio/video solution. Break-away flying leads and wall plates ensure flexible, efficient, high quality connections for all types of equipment.Ideal for educational and institutional installations, this wall plate receives PC video. Constructed from alum